 "title": "Sulfur Metabolism in S. cerevisiae and C. albicans",
 "summary": "This cluster revolves around the sulfur metabolism in Saccharomyces cerevisiae (S. cerevisiae) and Candida albicans (C. albicans). Key entities involved include genes and proteins such as Met32, Met17, and HSU1, which play crucial roles in sulfur metabolism. The cluster also highlights the importance of glutathione (GSH) in transporting Seo13 and the role of hydrogen sulfide (H2S) in utilizing C. albicans. Additionally, the cluster shows the relationship between sulfur metabolism and fermentation, with entities such as cysteine, homocysteine, and methionine being involved in this process.",
